WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.050
<b>Drawing Fun!</b>

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:03.490
Drawing!

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:04.670
F - U - N !

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:09.050
<b> Hubbub</b>

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:06.900
Big Sister Kisaragi!

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.050
Suneko-san!

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.190
Today we are doing a public 
filming at our local preschool!

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:17.600
Everybody! 
Please settle down!

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.030
Okay!

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.830
What a good response!

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.080
Today's theme: 
playing with boxes!

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:24.910
Any box is fine!

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:26.020
Like this one.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.010
Just drawing a face like this looks good!

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.000
I tried adding some decorations!

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.210
Now, everybody try!

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:34.940
Make whatever you like!

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.170
Okay!

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:37.330
And so,

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.450
<b> Gee Eh</b>

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:38.450
GA!

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.850
GA! Geijutsuka Art Design Class...

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:45.360
Is about to start!

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.400
Big Sister Kisaragi!

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:54.100
Kisaragi-dono.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:55.210
You're going to collide.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.260
GA's already begun!

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.840
Oh, did it start?

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:15.520
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.570
Oh, thanks, Kisaragi!

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:41.340
Sorry I couldn't find 
a cleaner drawing board.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:42.900
It's fine!

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.430
It's full of doodles, isn't it?

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:50.720
 Looking for a girlfriend

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:52.720
 Looking for a girlfriend

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:06.220
<b>A Happy Ending</b>

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:11.620
This is a story about a certain 
country in a certain world.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:16.950
It was a beautiful country 
of abundant color.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.810
However, there was a grey witch who 
was envious of the colorful land.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:26.950
And one day she stole all of 
the color from that country.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:32.840
The sky, the castle,
 the grass and the people

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:36.760
were all without color and 
it became a world of grey.

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:40.180
All except for a little red flower

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:42.450
which grew hidden in the forest

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:46.600
and a little girl born from that flower.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.170
...is the introduction. 
What do you think?

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:51.750
Seems fine.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.050
What introduction?

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:56.530
A picture drama?

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:57.300
Yup!

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.720
You know the Usubeni Preschool nearby?

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:04.300
Oh yeah. I've seen it 
on the way to school.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.270
About two bus stops before here.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:08.500
They'll sometimes 
come visit our campus

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.630
on field trips or walks, too.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:13.850
Well, that preschool asked us

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:17.670
if we'd make a paper 
drama for their story time.

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:20.860
What a heartwarming story!

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:22.190
By the way,

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:23.660
it appears that the middle school

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:25.760
and university also 
received similar requests.

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:29.790
Anyway, our club took the job 
without much consideration,

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:32.450
and it's become a project that 
we can't afford to give up on.

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:36.210
<b>Three Way Battle!!</b>

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:33.850
A three way battle?!

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:35.860
The preschool principal 
is a tactician!

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:39.060
So that's why you guys 
need to help out as well!

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:41.530
For writing the story 
and making the pictures.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:42.760
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:46.270
Well, I don't want to lose 
to middle schoolers, so...

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:49.290
Unusually, the club's 
pride has been swayed,

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:53.410
and Professor Tono has agreed to provide 
us with financial backing, too!

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:55.500
Oh wow! That really is unusual!

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:56.510
Leave me alone.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:58.990
Don't be surprised.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:01.250
The amount of 5,000 yen!

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.380
Hey, hey. Is that okay?

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:04.550
<b>Fret  fret</b>

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:06.110
5,000?!

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:07.590
That's the same amount as the

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:09.250
Fine Arts Club annual budget!

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.800
We can use whatever's
left over for the culture festival!

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:18.060
<b>Woo-hoo!</b>

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.790
Damn. I should've halved it.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:23.070
So, this is the story's heroine?

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.160
Right!

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:27.710
But, to be honest, this is about 
as far as I've thought it out.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:32.470
This ponytail reminds me of someone...

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:38.800
B-Buchi-san...

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.200
I-I'm sorry.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.490
I thought it looked like someone 
I knew so I instinctively...

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:44.500
Rather than redrawing it,

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:47.090
it'll be easier to just add glasses 
to the rest of the drawings.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:51.160
But honestly the president's story

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:53.280
doesn't even seem that interesting.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:54.900
Wait, really?

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:59.870
I wrote it with <i>The Thumb Princess</i> 
or <i>The Snow Queen</i> in mind.

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:03.630
Well, I don't really have much 
confidence in my story writing,

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.590
so if you have any suggestions 
I'll put them in.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:06.540
Let's see.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:08.270
Well, the story I was imagining

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:11.150
was much more action-adventure like.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:13.080
More like this!

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:15.620
More like what?!

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:16.370
What?

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:17.880
Doesn't it look like 
the final battle between

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.100
the heroine and the witch?

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:21.360
Those are supposed to 
be the same characters?!

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:24.570
Sorry I'm late!

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:26.630
Oh, you came, Tomokane.

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:29.620
Come help us out with 
the paper drama making.

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:31.220
Hmm? Paper drama?

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.740
What kind of story is it?

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:34.970
Like this!

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:38.080
Oh, a great war between monsters.

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:39.940
Sounds interesting.

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:41.170
Right?

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:42.600
So that's how he responds.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.590
All right, let's do it!

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:46.550
Okay.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:49.850
If we leave it to them, 
this will turn out terribly.

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:52.380
I've enlisted some unwanted help.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:55.710
Before they get out of control,

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:58.560
we'd better continue 
drawing and story writing.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:02.600
Then why don't we call 
for some help on our side.

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:03.770
Hmm? Who?

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:06.560
She's the kind of girl who 
probably likes this kind of stuff.

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:11.340
Hello?

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:30.090
<b>Actually, Cell Phone Use Is Prohibited</b>

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:15.190
I'm in the university library 
with my friends right now.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:18.110
No, I don't have anything 
particularly important going on...

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:19.700
Really?

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.990
Actually, we're in 
the middle of writing

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:23.500
Kisa-chan's biography in the Fine Arts Club.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:24.670
Can you help?

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:27.920
What exactly is your club doing to me?!

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:30.090
Kisaragi, shhh!

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:36.100
So that's what you were talking about.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:38.250
Oh, you meant this girl.

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:40.160
That's right.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:43.000
Hey Kisa-chan, what kind 
of story would you write?

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:45.230
Let's see...

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:49.800
How about the girl goes out and looks

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:51.650
for other colored friends?

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:54.830
I'd be lonely all by myself, so...

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:55.890
I see.

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.710
The idea of searching for color

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.490
could make for an interesting 
visual presentation.

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:04.520
Then, once they've 
assembled all the colors,

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:06.730
they head into a deadly battle 
with the witch, right?!

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:10.780
You can just ignore what he says.

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:14.140
Tomokane, have you made 
something like this before?

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:16.610
Not picture stories,

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:19.180
but I've made a lot of 
different books with effects.

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.410
The other day I had some time 
in the nurse's office

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:22.860
and I made something.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:25.690
I think it's in this 
sketchbook somewhere...

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.190
Oh! I wanna see!

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:30.690
Oh! A pop-up book!

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:37.120
Oh, that's a sketch from 
the nurse's office,

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.800
since I'm there more than 
I'm in the art room...

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:42.380
I really thought it might 
jump out for a second!

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:43.940
My heart from my mouth that is!

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:47.730
GA!

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.660
Kisaragi-chan, you're a GA student,

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:54.590
so I can trust you to finish 
these pictures, right?

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:56.320
I've done the rough sketch.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:57.850
M-Me?

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.380
Finish it completely?

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:04.700
As she went toward the voice, 
there was a small pond.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:06.920
Though it was small,

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:11.120
it was the blue blue color 
that the sky used to be.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:13.300
“Is anybody there?”

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:17.450
The girl peered into the pond.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:22.620
And there, about the same 
size as her, was a small...

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:28.710
Did the story become a premium 
channel from this point on?

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:30.270
There's a lot of noise.

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:33.140
You don't have to be so nervous.

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:35.720
S-Sorry! I'm sorry!

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:39.950
Here, Kisa-chan. 
Find the yellow.

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:41.460
Um...

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:42.960
I made scenes like this one

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:46.230
where the kids have to find things.

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:50.080
Now, where could it be?

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:51.380
There! There!

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:54.200
I used to like these, as well!

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:58.900
Hmm? A page where you 
have to find something?

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:01.970
Apparently, it's how you get 
the kids involved in the story!

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:04.570
Oh, that? In that case, 
we've already made some.

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:05.380
Really?

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:12.200
Since the characters 
are so inconsistent,

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:14.200
they've become a 
spot-the-difference game.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:16.260
At least do something about

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:17.800
your urge to draw by feeling only.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:21.230
Could these girls here

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:23.720
be modeled after your 
friends, Kisaragi-chan?

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.670
Oh, yes!

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:28.790
As I was drawing, they just turned 
out like this before I knew it!

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:30.690
Is that so?

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:33.540
Kisa-chan, you really do like 
your friends, don't you?

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:36.650
Hey, Buchi-san.

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:39.220
What do you think of a 
story modeled after me?

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:41.810
What kind of story do 
you think it would be?

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:54.180
<b> Hi-ya!</b>

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:45.060
Journey to the West?

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:54.180
<b> Hurrr</b>

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:48.350
No, no. It would be Kintarou.

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:49.310
Right?

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:53.670
I finally understand how you all see me.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:59.240
Finally, the girl arrived 
at the witch's lair.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.870
She began to worry 
whether she'd be able

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:04.410
to return all the world's color.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:08.040
But the girl had with
 her all the friends

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.500
she'd made along the way.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:12.470
As long as they were together,

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:15.370
even the grey witch 
couldn't scare them.

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:17.480
Couldn't... scare them...

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:21.950
Who was it who sent 
creatures into our world?!

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.220
My bad. I drew it wrong.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:26.510
Awara. You're a creature, as well.

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:31.370
And?

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:34.260
Did you give the preschool 
your paper drama?

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:35.870
Oh, yup.

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:37.740
Yesterday, when I went with

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:39.220
Homura and Uozumi down to the preschool

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:40.320
to read the paper drama,

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:42.550
they gave me this handmade thing.

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:42.380
Given

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:45.850
It seems like the preschoolers 
really liked it.

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:48.650
Oh really? That's great.

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:50.210
It suits you!

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:54.720
Leave it to me... or rather...

00:11:55.510 --> 00:12:10.960
<b> What is that?! 
What's that weird thing?!</b>

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:59.530
What is that?! What's that weird thing?!

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:03.610
Like I said! This one 
is the witch and...

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:05.850
What they really got excited about

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:08.490
wasn't the paper drama,

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:09.740
but Homura's pictures
 and presentation.

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:10.880
That's just how it is.

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:12.860
Hey, hey, Kisaragi-chan.

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:14.550
What's this picture?

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:16.990
The other day when I helped

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:19.300
my friend make their 
paper drama,

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.600
they gave me a copy 
of one of the pages.

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:23.340
But with just this picture,

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:25.560
it's hard to tell what 
kind of story it was.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:28.390
Once upon a time, in a faraway place,

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:32.490
there was a beautiful 
and colorful land...

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:34.070
Oh, it's starting.

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:38.290
Yes, until something terrible happened.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:39.360
The end!

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:40.860
That's an intro!

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.220
Don't end it there!

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:44.840
But it's kind of accurate.

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:48.080
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:53.080
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:50.200
What's this weird thing!

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:51.100
Like I said!

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:52.770
This one is the witch and...

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:58.070
This mobile crepe shop 
was on TV yesterday.

00:12:58.350 --> 00:13:00.210
Wow. So it's popular.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:02.230
Let's go next time!

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:06.990
Making a list of things 
to buy in your phone?

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:08.560
Yes.

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:11.150
While I still remember them, after class.

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:12.070
Shopping?

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:13.280
Are you going to the school shop?

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:16.240
No, I'm going to the art supply store.

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:18.430
I heard they're having a sale, so...

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:19.740
I see.

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:22.940
Since it's cheap, maybe I 
ought to buy something as well.

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:23.990
To stock up.

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:25.640
Then, let's go!

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:27.520
It'll be more fun with everyone!

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:28.620
Yes!

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:29.720
Yes!

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:32.770
In that case, I definitely won't 
buy anything, but can I come?

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:33.430
Yes.

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:36.720
I don't even know where 
you're going, but can I come?

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:37.730
Yes.

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.470
Kisaragi, do you go to this store often?

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:44.200
Yes, since I use up 
materials so quickly.

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:46.230
This month I was trying

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:47.920
to save my allowance,

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:49.970
so it's really helpful that 
they're having a sale.

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:52.450
Is money tight this month?

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:54.140
Or rather,

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.060
there was something I wanted to do, so...

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:57.930
What? Something you wanted to do?!

00:13:57.930 --> 00:13:59.950
What? What? Learn something? 
Studying abroad?

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:02.180
Or, what, dating?
 Breast enhancement?

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:03.750
What are you thinking, Kisaragi?!

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:06.120
Your father didn't approve that!

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:07.040
Approve what?

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:09.100
Now your cheeks are turning red!

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:21.150
Wow. Acrylic, watercolor, 
pencils, pigment, palettes.

00:14:21.150 --> 00:14:22.600
They've got everything!

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:26.540
Just looking at all this is so exciting!

00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:30.050
They have so many more 
supplies than at school!

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:34.240
I feel like I'm in 
a magical supply shop.

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:38.790
{text follows} Does Cadmium Yellow have cadmium in it?

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:42.770
{text follows}Apparently, oil based paints 
have poisonous ingredients.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:45.600
<b>Witches?</b>

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:50.810
{text follows}Leathac, Canson, Mermaid...

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:52.950
Ah! They even have Edokozome!

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:55.110
<b> Magic Spells?</b>

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:57.490
I wonder where the modeling paste is.

00:14:58.070 --> 00:14:59.740
I think it's just past here.

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:04.020
Ooh! This colored pencil's 
color is really nice!

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:13.040
These modeling dolls always get put 
into really weird poses, don't they?

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:16.590
Wow! These are super cute!

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:17.950
Fruits, Animals, Flowers, Sweets, Butterflies.

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:17.960
I think I'll buy some!

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:20.270
Hey, Tomokane. Put out 
your hand for a second.

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:22.970
I'm getting one of each, okay?

00:15:22.970 --> 00:15:25.870
What? Wait. What are these?

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:27.610
What are these for?

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:28.930
They're clips!

00:15:28.930 --> 00:15:31.450
For holding and organizing paper.

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:35.210
Recently they've come out 
with all kinds of shapes.

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:36.500
Really?

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:39.480
Wow!

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:46.470
Wait. Don't you usually 
use this acrylic?

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:48.560
Yes, but...

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:50.260
See?

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.530
<b>Acrylic paint 
all colors</b>

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.530
<b> Original Retail Price
 284 yen
(Actual Price 270 yen)</b>

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.530
<b>198 yen</b>

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.530
<b> Actual Price 189 yen</b>

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:56.010
This brand is much cheaper today.

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:57.540
Oh, you're right.

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:01.460
You can buy seven for the price of five!

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:05.710
I figured I'd buy the 
colors that I use up fastest.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.170
Good idea.

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:09.850
Even when you only have one color 
missing, it's a real hassle.

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:13.490
Scarlet and... yellow and...

00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:17.620
White and white and white and white.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:23.350
 Plop plop plop

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:19.860
How much white do you use?!

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:21.340
Then I'll need...

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:23.360
Leave it, Masa! Everyone already 
knows what you get!

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:26.860
Nakagawa, Nasu, Nazuka, Nadabame, 
Narigami, Nogami, Noda, Noto
Nomura, Hamaguchi, Hamada, Hayama, Harima, Handa

00:16:24.110 --> 00:16:26.860
Nozaki... Nozaki...

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:28.610
Yamaguchi...

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:30.980
Tomokane, put out your hand!

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:32.870
Hmm? Again?

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:36.770
There! Tomokane, you should 
try a little harder!

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:36.770
Try a little harder

00:16:36.770 --> 00:16:39.510
Now you've done it!

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:42.860
In return, I'll stamp 
something on your forehead.

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:40.480
<b>Crash</b>

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:42.600
<b>Crash</b>

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:43.860
My forehead?!

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:45.880
<b>Returned goods</b>

00:16:44.860 --> 00:16:45.880
Returned goods, or...

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:47.620
<b>Handle with Caution</b>

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:47.620
Handle with Caution?

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:48.500
Which do you prefer?

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:53.890
Returned goods
Handle with Caution

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:51.300
What about “Payable at Bank”?

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:53.880
Payable at Bank

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:53.890
I don't want any of them!

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:58.000
Tracing paper: 600 yen for 50 sheets.

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.300
Tracing paper sure is expensive.

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:04.580
I won't be able to buy it
this time right now, so...

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:06.600
I'll go with the 
“secret technique."

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:07.810
“Secret Technique”?

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:11.170
Isn't this the letter supply section?

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:12.430
That's right.

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:15.020
Ahh, here it is.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:18.010
Air mail paper?

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:21.070
This is only 200 yen for 60 sheets.

00:17:24.610 --> 00:17:26.960
Wow. This is a lot like tracing paper.

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:32.220
Compared to the real thing, 
it's a bit harder to use,

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:34.880
but it's good for practicing on.

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:36.230
Amazing.

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:37.690
Confidential

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:37.700
Look, look!

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.680
It's in a glass case!

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:42.710
Whoa! An expensive looking paint set!

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:45.080
Wow, 170,000 yen!

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:47.860
I wonder if it's the wooden 
box that's so expensive.

00:17:47.860 --> 00:17:49.950
What?! Look at this, Tomokane!

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:54.120
The inside looks like this!

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:56.950
Whoa! What an amazing final form!

00:17:56.950 --> 00:17:58.260
Full options?!

00:17:58.470 --> 00:17:59.850
Mother!

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:01.610
I want this, I want this!

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:04.270
Buy me this “super 
equipped Gazai-der”!

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:05.310
Mother!

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:07.330
Who are you calling "mother"?!

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:08.230
“Gazaider”?

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:08.480
 Gazaider?!

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:12.610
Gazaider!

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:14.770
That kind of robot does not exist!

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:17.350
Here, Kisaragi-chan, look!
 Look at this!

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:21.550
What?! It costs 100,000 yen!

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:25.850
But wouldn't it be wonderful 
to paint something with this?

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:29.760
Like a female art student 
at an art academy.

00:18:30.350 --> 00:18:32.170
Like they used to in Paris...

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:37.870
To take out your canvas and paints,

00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:40.030
and paint the scene that 
is captured in your heart.

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:46.880
These colored pencils cost 4,000 yen~

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:51.960
These watercolors cost 6,000 yen~

00:18:53.390 --> 00:18:57.800
These oil paints cost 14,000 yen~

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:00.450
And I can't use any of them!

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:03.570
Are commoners prohibited 
from enjoying even

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:05.040
a simulated experience?

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:10.150
Oh! I know. I'll buy 
a notebook for class.

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:13.260
In that case, get me one, too.

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:14.200
Okay!

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:16.750
Yes! Namiko-san, Namiko-san.

00:19:17.190 --> 00:19:19.780
Where are the notebooks 
you'd use for class?

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:23.300
Turn here and they'll 
be on your left hand side.

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:24.620
Thanks!

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:28.060
 Doodle Pads

00:19:28.490 --> 00:19:30.530
Noda-chan, are you guys 
getting notebooks, as well?

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:33.000
Yup. We are.

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.810
See? Look. There used to 
be a cat on the old zodiac!

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:40.610
Then, why don't we buy 
this 4-pack together?

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:42.220
I'm buying two, so...

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:42.930
Sure.

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:44.640
Oh, thrifty!

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:47.820
That will be 571 yen.

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:50.770
Please draw one from this box.

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:53.370
Apparently you can draw once 
for purchases over 500 yen

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:56.540
and twice for purchases over 1000 yen.

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:57.760
Could it be?

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:59.160
Yup, thrifty. {same as text}

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:02.050
Oh, no! That's not it!

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:05.460
They do this lottery every 
time there's a sale,

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:08.070
but I've never won anything.

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:08.070
It comes to 1420 yen.

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:10.020
Then, can I draw?

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:12.400
Namiko-san, what'd you draw?

00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:13.790
"Please try again."

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:15.940
Low Grade Goods

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:15.960
But I got a highlighter.

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:20.210
Oh, if it's a pen then we 
can't exactly divide it up.

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:22.630
If that's the case, then 
I'll let you guys have it.

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:23.760
This and this!

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:26.620
This is the second prize.

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:28.640
A stationery voucher worth 1500 yen.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:30.740
Whaat?! {text same}

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:36.640
Are you sure you're okay

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:38.750
with giving us the stationery voucher?

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:41.720
Of course. After all, you 
were trying so hard to save.

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:43.500
No, no. It's fine.

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:45.760
Besides, you treated me to this instead.

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:47.960
So I've already completed my mission.

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:49.350
Mission?

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:53.690
This crepe shop is really 
popular these days, right?

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:56.310
I was hoping to come here with everyone!

00:20:56.670 --> 00:20:57.690
So that's why.

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:00.620
All right, Kisaragi. 
Since today's special,

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:02.710
I'll give you <i>two</i> bites 
of my tuna ham salad!

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:03.380
Eat it!

00:21:03.380 --> 00:21:05.040
I already ate mine.

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:08.020
But you can have three bites of 
Namiko-san's chocolate custard!

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:09.630
Don't decide for other people!

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:12.410
Masa, did you draw a lottery as well?

00:21:12.970 --> 00:21:13.680
Yes.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:17.160
Oh. So, what did you buy?

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:19.060
This and that.

00:21:21.230 --> 00:21:24.100
All right! Does anyone need a pasteboard?

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:26.280
Oh, one please.

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:27.550
I already have one.

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:30.610
I have one in the classroom, 
but I want one!

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:32.100
You lazy bum.

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:33.360
Combine!

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:35.110
Gazaider!

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:36.870
{text follows} Stop messing around.

00:21:37.840 --> 00:21:39.810
Huh? This pasteboard...

00:21:41.140 --> 00:21:42.670
It's the one from before!

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:43.710
<b> Slide</b>

00:21:46.190 --> 00:21:47.240
What a big family...

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:40.900
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:26.200 --> 00:23:28.910
The water pipe appears 
to have been busted.

00:23:28.910 --> 00:23:32.150
I only put a little strength 
into turning the faucet...

00:23:32.150 --> 00:23:35.160
Is everything all right? 
You three are soaking wet.

00:23:35.160 --> 00:23:37.150
I'm getting a weird chill.

00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:40.900
Hexenkessel

00:23:37.150 --> 00:23:38.250
Let's have a hot pot!

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:39.560
Let's have a hot pot!
